# Agent Guidelines

Before taking action in a new session, read this entire file and any applicable repository `AGENTS.md` files. Check the relevant instructions before launching terminals, creating tmux windows, changing configuration, or opening applications. Do not rely on remembered conventions when the current instructions are available.

After fixing a problem, document the symptom, cause, solution, and how the fix was verified, including relevant machine or version differences. Update the project's existing troubleshooting or setup notes; create a concise topic-specific document when needed. Keep dotfile and Neovim fix notes in the chezmoi source repository, such as `docs/nvim/troubleshooting.md`. Keep small fixes brief, extend existing notes, and correct outdated guidance so we gradually build a useful collection of verified fixes without duplicating explanations.

When launching user terminals or tmux from agent tools, remove agent-injected environment overrides such as `NO_COLOR` from the child environment and verify inheritance; a new tmux server retains them for later sessions.

When creating a tmux window, let tmux choose the index according to its active `base-index` setting. Omit `-t` when the current session is appropriate; to select a session explicitly, use `-t 'session-name:'` with the trailing colon and no window index. For example, `tmux new-window -t '0:'` selects session `0` and assigns the window index automatically, while `tmux new-window -t 0` explicitly requests window index `0`. Never force a window index unless the user requests it. This user's tmux configuration starts window and pane numbering at `1`.

When asked to copy text to the user's clipboard from an agent session inside tmux, use `tmux set-buffer -w 'text'` (with proper shell quoting), rather than printing OSC 52 escape sequences to captured tool output. This method was verified to reach the macOS clipboard through Ghostty, a local tmux, SSH, and a remote tmux. It relies on OSC 52 clipboard forwarding being configured through the terminal chain; a successful command alone does not prove clipboard delivery on a new setup. Remote `wl-copy` does not target the Mac's clipboard. Copying does not execute the text.

Previous Oh My Pi chats are locally preserved. When they are relevant, search prompts in `~/.omp/agent/history.db` and read full transcripts under `~/.omp/agent/sessions/`; `history://` lists harness-registered agents, not the interactive-session archive.

{{- if eq .chezmoi.os "darwin" }}

For the user's OrbStack/Linux coursework setup and terminal-based tutoring preferences, read `~/.agents/BI-UOS/orbstack-setup.md` and `~/.agents/BI-UOS/progress.md`. Keep environment notes in the setup file and append dated learning checkpoints to the progress file. Before answering their shell questions, inspect the current user terminal pane; explain the actual situation briefly without changing their input.
{{- end }}

{{- if and (eq .chezmoi.os "linux") (eq .chezmoi.osRelease.id "arch") }}

When launching GUI applications (e.g. Xournal++), run them detached from the agent process tree using `systemd-run --user <app> "<file>"`.

When asked to open a directory in LazyVim in another Kitty, launch a separate Kitty with `systemd-run --user`, start a new project-named tmux session inside it, and run `lazy-nvim .` from that directory; do not create a window in the current tmux session. Ordinary `nvim` selects the default native base configuration, not LazyVim.

## Xournal++ Notes
- **Location**: Notes repository is at `~/stasbebra2006/Xournal/` (academic subjects in `subjects/<SUBJECT>/`, e.g. `PKM` for BI-PKM).
- **New Files**: Always create the `.xopp` file before launching (Xournal++ errors on non-existent paths).
  - Inspect current template settings from `~/.config/xournalpp/settings.xml` under property `pageTemplate` (contains `size=WIDTHxHEIGHT`, `backgroundType`, and `backgroundColor`). Alternatively, inspect `<page>` and `<background>` from the most recent `.xopp` in the subject folder.
  - Write a valid gzip-compressed XML document: `<xournal creator="xournalpp ..."><page width="WIDTH" height="HEIGHT"><background type="solid" color="COLORff" style="TYPE"/><layer/></page></xournal>`.
{{- end }}
